I didn't add the `http-client` import. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, and the spec says that clause is its entire authority. Also, `RunInfo` has no text field (only `date` and `started`), so there is no "input's text" to send. The node below is the state-read-only version, which keeps the `urls` output unchanged. If the platform team does approve widening the grant, that needs a change to the graph's `with` clause, and the enrichment input needs a defined source.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
//! LoadSubscriptions: reads the `subscriptions` store and returns the URL list.
//!
//! Capability: `StateHandle<'subscriptions', read>` only (`aap:caps/state-read`).
//! The `http-client` import was intentionally not added; see the note on
//! `enrich` below.
//!
//! Stored format: under `STATE_KEY`, one URL per line. Blank lines are dropped.
//! Output always contains a `urls` field (possibly empty), which satisfies
//! `ensures present(urls)`.

wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use aap::caps::state_read;

/// Key within the `subscriptions` store that holds the newline-separated URL list.
const STATE_KEY: &str = "urls";

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = state_read::get(STATE_KEY)
            .map(|raw| parse_urls(&raw))
            .unwrap_or_default();

        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

/// Splits the stored text into one URL per non-blank line.
fn parse_urls(raw: &str) -> Vec<String> {
    raw.lines()
        .map(str::trim)
        .filter(|line| !line.is_empty())
        .map(String::from)
        .collect()
}

// Note on the requested enrichment fetch: it is not implemented. Adding
// `aap:caps/http-client` would widen this node beyond its declared
// `with` clause (state-read only). Also, `RunInfo` has no text field, so
// `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=<text>` has no input to
// interpolate.

export!(Node);
```

